# How compiled languages (C, C++, Java, Kotlin, C#, Go, Rust, Scala, Dart,
# Ruby, PHP, Swift) are run. Python, R, SQL, HTML, JS and TS always run in
# the browser and need none of this.

# Option 1 — self-hosted Piston (recommended): sandboxed, open source.
# RUNNER_BACKEND=piston
# PISTON_URL=http://localhost:2000

# Option 2 — Judge0 (self-hosted CE, or the RapidAPI plan with a key).
# RUNNER_BACKEND=judge0
# JUDGE0_URL=https://judge0-ce.p.rapidapi.com
# JUDGE0_KEY=your-rapidapi-key

# Option 3 — local toolchains, DEVELOPMENT ONLY (no sandbox). This is the
# default in `npm run dev` when nothing else is configured; it is refused in
# production unless you also set ALLOW_UNSAFE_LOCAL_RUNNER=1.
# RUNNER_BACKEND=local
